.TH MINISNIFFER 1 "2026-07-09" "MiniSniffer 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
MiniSniffer \- small C packet sniffer and network analyzer built on libpcap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B MiniSniffer
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B MiniSniffer
captures live packets or reads an offline pcap file, parses common IPv4/IPv6
link-layer formats, applies protocol/port/host/payload/application filters,
prints readable packet summaries or JSON Lines, optionally writes CSV logs or
a new pcap file, and can report capture statistics when the run completes.
.PP
MiniSniffer is for learning, local diagnostics, and authorized network
observation. It does not decrypt encrypted traffic, inject or modify packets,
or attempt to evade detection.
.PP
Live packet capture usually requires elevated operating-system permissions
(commonly running as root, e.g. with
.BR sudo ).
Reading with
.B \-\-read
does not require elevated permissions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the MiniSniffer version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-interfaces
List libpcap capture devices with descriptions, address hints, and
default-candidate markers.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " name"
Capture from a specific interface, such as
.IR en0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-count " number"
Stop after this many displayed packets. If omitted, capture continues until
Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress startup and stop summaries. Packet output and errors still print.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print the full startup configuration summary before capture.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable terminal color output. Current MiniSniffer output is plain text.
.TP
.BI \-\-protocol " tcp|udp|icmp|arp|other"
Display only packets matching the selected protocol.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " number"
Display only TCP/UDP packets where the source or destination port matches.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ip"
Display only packets where the source or destination IPv4 or IPv6 address
matches.
.TP
.B \-\-payload
Print a bounded hex and ASCII payload preview for displayed packets.
.TP
.BI \-\-payload-bytes " number"
Set the payload preview length. Default is 256 bytes. Maximum is 256 bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-payload-decode-bytes " number"
Set the payload decode window used by payload filters and packet-local app
decoders. Default is 2048 bytes. Maximum is 65535 bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-payload-contains " text"
Display only packets whose bounded payload decode window contains the literal
text.
.TP
.BI \-\-payload-hex " hex"
Display only packets whose bounded payload decode window contains the byte
pattern. Hex patterns may include spaces, colons, or hyphens as separators.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Write displayed packets to a CSV file. The path must not already exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-read " file.pcap"
Read packets from an offline pcap file instead of live capture. Does not
require interface selection or capture permissions.
.TP
.BI \-\-write " file.pcap"
Write displayed packets to a new pcap file, preserving timestamps and link
type. Existing files are refused.
.TP
.B \-\-no-bpf
Disable kernel-level BPF pre-filtering and rely entirely on software
filtering. Useful for debugging filter behavior.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print displayed packets as JSON Lines instead of human-readable packet text.
.TP
.BI \-\-flush-log " always|line|exit"
Control CSV flush timing. Default is
.IR line ,
preserving row-by-row safe behavior.
.TP
.B \-\-decode-app
Decode packet-local HTTP, DNS, TLS ClientHello, DHCP, mDNS, and conservative
QUIC Initial-packet metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-reassemble
Enable bounded TCP stream reassembly for app decoding. Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-max-flows " number"
Set the maximum number of tracked TCP flows for reassembly. Default is 512;
maximum is 1024. Requires
.BR \-\-reassemble .
.TP
.BI \-\-stream-buffer-bytes " number"
Set the per-direction TCP stream buffer cap. Default is 32768 bytes; maximum
is 1048576 bytes. Requires
.BR \-\-reassemble .
.TP
.BI \-\-flow-timeout " seconds"
Evict flows idle for at least this many seconds. Default is 60 seconds.
Requires
.BR \-\-reassemble .
.TP
.BI \-\-app " http|dns|tls|dhcp|mdns|quic"
Display only packets with decoded app metadata for the selected protocol.
Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-http-host " host"
Display only decoded HTTP packets with a matching Host header. Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-http-method " method"
Display only decoded HTTP requests with a matching method. Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-dns-query " name"
Display only decoded DNS or mDNS packets with a matching first query name.
Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-dns-type " type"
Display only decoded DNS or mDNS packets with a matching first query type,
such as
.I A
or
.IR AAAA .
Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-tls-sni " host"
Display only decoded TLS ClientHello packets with a matching SNI hostname.
Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-tls-alpn " protocol"
Display only decoded TLS ClientHello packets advertising the ALPN protocol.
Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-dhcp-type " type"
Display only decoded DHCP packets with a matching message type, such as
.IR discover ", " offer ", " request ", or " ack .
Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-quic-version " version"
Display only decoded QUIC Initial packets with a matching version, decimal or
0x-prefixed hex. Requires
.BR \-\-decode-app .
.TP
.BI \-\-domain-match " normalized|exact|idna"
Set HTTP Host, DNS query, and TLS SNI domain matching mode. Default is
.IR normalized .
.I idna
requires a build made with
.BR WITH_LIBIDN2=1 .
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print displayed packet totals after capture completes.
.SH EXAMPLES
Capture five displayed packets on the automatically selected interface:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo MiniSniffer \-\-count 5
.EE
.RE
.PP
Capture TCP packets and print stats at the end:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo MiniSniffer \-\-protocol tcp \-\-count 20 \-\-stats
.EE
.RE
.PP
Read an existing capture file, no elevated permissions required:
.PP
.RS
.EX
MiniSniffer \-\-read capture.pcap \-\-protocol tcp \-\-count 10 \-\-stats
.EE
.RE
.PP
Decode and filter HTTP requests by Host header:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo MiniSniffer \-\-decode-app \-\-app http \-\-http-host example.com
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
CSV logs written with
.B \-\-log
are created atomically with owner-only permissions (0600); existing files and
symbolic links are refused.
.PP
Pcap files written with
.B \-\-write
must not already exist; MiniSniffer creates them exclusively.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B MiniSniffer
exits with a non-zero status on invalid arguments, interface errors, or
capture failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR pcap (3)
.PP
Full documentation, including the TCP reassembly model, BPF pre-filtering
scope, and CSV/JSON schemas:
.br
https://github.com/finn-abel/PacketScope
.SH BUGS
Report issues at the project's GitHub issue tracker.
.SH AUTHOR
MiniSniffer contributors.
